# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Chikashi Shinagawa et al. (2026). Matlantis-PFP v8: Universal Machine Learning Interatomic Potential with Better Experimental Agreements via r2SCAN Functional.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2603.11063  arXiv:2603.11063v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2603.11063v2 (sha256 20772a2cb51160a5...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 265 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/shinagawa2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: PFP v8 (TeaNet architecture) trained jointly on the new
# PFP-R2SCAN data set, the PFP-PBE/PBE+U and PFP-WB97XD data sets and OC20
# through calculation-mode labels, with its formation-energy MAEs against
# experiment (Table 3) and surface-energy MAEs against experiment (Table
# 5) per calculation mode. GMTKN55 WTMAD-2 scores (Table 4) are weighted
# deviations, not plain MAEs, and melting-point MAEs are in K; neither is
# encoded. DFT reference rows of Tables 3-5 are not MLIP results.

