###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# r2SCAN calculations take about four times longer than PBE; the PFP-R2SCAN
# data set took about one year to build (the PFP-PBE/+U set about five
# years). No training or inference times are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - PFP v8 is one model with calculation modes (R2SCAN, PBE, PBE+U, WB97XD and +D3 variants); the run records PFP-R2SCAN as its data set and the other three data sets are listed separately. Data-set sizes are given only to one significant figure (Table 1) and are kept in the labels. PFP v8 is not a registry model.
# - GMTKN55 WTMAD-2 scores (Table 4; e.g. 9.28 kcal/mol for R2SCAN+D3) are weighted deviations and are not encoded as MAE; surface-energy MBE and MAPE (Table 5) and melting-point MAEs (133 K and 279 K, Fig. 4) have no metric type or unit in the schema.
# - The cutoff of the last two graph-convolution layers is 0.9 nm (0.6 nm before v8); other architecture settings are not stated. The D3(BJ) correction (14 A cutoff, torch-dftd) is added outside the network.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/shinagawa2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

